540 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (A prime example of how Data Science, Machine Learning \(ML\), and Natural Language Processing \(NLP\) can transform modern hiring and selection practices is the "Hiring Driven by Data Insights of the Applicants" project. Traditional hiring methods mostly depend on human judgment processes, manual CV screening, and subjective evaluation all of which are time-consuming and prone to unconscious bias. In order to increase hiring's effectiveness, impartiality, and equity, this project has successfully conceived and developed an alternative, data-driven recruitment model. This work's primary achievement is the development of a data-driven hiring pipeline that reads, evaluates, and analyzes resumes using ML and NLP algorithms. By converting unstructured resume data into structured, analyzable information, the project enables the automatic extraction of significant applicant attributes such as accomplishments, education, experience, and skills. A "Resume Score," which indicates how well a candidate fits a particular role, is created by comparing these extracted features with particular job requirements. The likelihood of hiring success or candidate-job fit is then predicted using this score as input for machine learning classifiers like Random Forest, Logistic Regression, and Linear Regression. The results of the model demonstrate how data-driven screening practices can significantly improve the accuracy and reliability of hiring decisions. For instance, Random Forest classifiers can capture complex, non-linear relationships between candidate attributes and hiring outcomes thanks to their ensemble learning methodology. On the other hand, HR professionals can use logistic regression's easily understandable probability results to inform their final decisions. )
/E (A prime example of how Data Science, Machine Learning \(ML\), and Natural Language Processing \(NLP\) can transform modern hiring and selection practices is the "Hiring Driven by Data Insights of the Applicants" project. Traditional hiring methods mostly depend on human judgment processes, manual CV screening, and subjective evaluation all of which are time-consuming and prone to unconscious bias. In order to increase hiring's effectiveness, impartiality, and equity, this project has successfully conceived and developed an alternative, data-driven recruitment model. This work's primary achievement is the development of a data-driven hiring pipeline that reads, evaluates, and analyzes resumes using ML and NLP algorithms. By converting unstructured resume data into structured, analyzable information, the project enables the automatic extraction of significant applicant attributes such as accomplishments, education, experience, and skills. A "Resume Score," which indicates how well a candidate fits a particular role, is created by comparing these extracted features with particular job requirements. The likelihood of hiring success or candidate-job fit is then predicted using this score as input for machine learning classifiers like Random Forest, Logistic Regression, and Linear Regression. The results of the model demonstrate how data-driven screening practices can significantly improve the accuracy and reliability of hiring decisions. For instance, Random Forest classifiers can capture complex, non-linear relationships between candidate attributes and hiring outcomes thanks to their ensemble learning methodology. On the other hand, HR professionals can use logistic regression's easily understandable probability results to inform their final decisions. )
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [1 2 3 4]
>>
endobj
